Z||000001||Joe Torma||11-22-2001||01:29 AM||||Decent idea...I've seen them for outdoor use too.  Desicant stuff should work.<P>But I've got lots of work to do on my car!!! So I got one of those instant garages.  11x20'  Its a perfect size for the Fiero. $350 at BJ's.  Got a tarp for a floor that I will velcro to the sides to wind proof(under front & back-the sides have extra material)<P>I even wired up a flourecent light in it.  Got a few more to do too.  Unfortunately, I still have to bundle up, but at least there's no wind!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||11-22-2001||06:33 AM||||Looks pretty good.  If you have the $$$, I've seen one in the British old car mags that has a little fan and filter to refresh the air constantly.<P>Gary<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||CoolBlue87GT||11-22-2001||08:41 AM||||Winter ?  What's that ? I moved to Florida, & that solved my winter problem !!  lol<P>That bag cover looks good.  <P>I remember when living in Maryland, I rented a 3 bay wood garage & stored two cars it.<P>There were a few perfect winter days, when I took the Fiero out. <P>Nothing like a ride on a crisp winter day in a nice clean car, when everyone else drives past with a salt covered car.<P>They look over & wish theirs looked so good.!<P>Ah winter.||||reg||6
Z||000004||Fred88GT||11-22-2001||11:17 AM||||I have a 1926 Model T Ford that I have stored <BR>inside an enclosed trailer every winter for <BR>10 years. I have been using a different brand<BR>of bag with desiccant. When the car comes out <BR>in the spring it looks just like when it went<BR>in. This fall I purchased a new bag from<BR>carbag with the zipper. It was a whole lot <BR>easier to use than the  one I had before.<BR>Carbag recomends that you have a regular car<BR>cover to put over the car before you put it <BR>in the bag. I have never used one for a Fiero<BR>This product gets a thumbs up from me.<P>Fred<P>85GT<BR>88GT<BR>||||reg||1
